    <statement><p>It is given to you that an equation of the tangent line to the graph
of <m>y=g(x)</m> at <m>x = 4</m> is
<me>2 x + 10 y = -12</me>
It follows that <m>y =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/> is the equation of the tangent line
to <m>y = g(x^2)</m> at <m>x = 2</m></p>
<p>and that <m>y =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/> is the equation
of the tangent line to <m>y = \left(g(x)\right)^2</m> at <m>x = 4</m>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-0.8\mathopen{}\left(x-2\right)+-2</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.8\mathopen{}\left(x-4\right)+\left(-2\right)^{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
